1.bug_scenario:
When formatting a TypeScript generic declaration with an empty tuple type as a conditional check, Prettier (v2.5.0) inserts a stray comma inside the empty brackets when the entire line exactly meets the print-width boundary. In our repro, the long identifier and a 120-column limit pushes the `aaddffgg extends []` tuple pattern onto its own indented lines. Instead of printing `[]`, it renders it as `[
  ,
]`, inserting an unwanted comma.
